Spec: Array Operations

Purpose:
  Create grid (rectangular) and circular arrays of selected shapes
  for efficient multi-piece sheet layouts.

Owns:
  ./array.ts
  ./array.test.ts

Must:
  Grid array creates rows × columns copies with specified X/Y spacing.
  Circular array creates N copies evenly distributed around a center point.
  Original shapes are preserved (copies are new shapes).
  All copies are added to the store via a single undoable command.
  Grid array spacing is in mm (converted to pixels internally).
  Circular array rotates copies to face outward (optional).

Must not:
  Modify original shapes.
  Create more than 1000 copies in a single operation (guard against OOM).
  Operate on empty selection.

Depends on:
  @IShape
  @useStore
  @Geometry

Exposes:
  GridArrayCommand(shapes, rows, columns, spacingX, spacingY)
  CircularArrayCommand(shapes, count, center, radius, rotateItems)

Accepts:
  shapes: IShape[] (source shapes to array)
  rows: number (1-50)
  columns: number (1-50)
  spacingX: number (mm)
  spacingY: number (mm)
  count: number (2-100)
  center: Point
  radius: number (mm)
  rotateItems: boolean

Scenario: 3x4 grid array
  Given one rectangle (20mm × 10mm) is selected
  When the user creates a 3×4 grid with spacing 5mm × 5mm
  Then 12 rectangles appear in a 3-column, 4-row grid
  And spacing between edges is 5mm horizontally and 5mm vertically
  And the original rectangle is preserved at its position

Scenario: circular array of 6
  Given one star shape is selected
  When the user creates a circular array of 6 around the material center
  Then 6 copies appear evenly spaced (60° apart) around the center
  And each copy is rotated to face outward

Scenario: undo array
  Given a grid array of 9 shapes was just created
  When the user presses Ctrl+Z
  Then only the original shape remains
  And the 9 copies are removed

Tasks:
  [ ] Create GridArrayCommand class.
  [ ] Create CircularArrayCommand class.
  [ ] Implement clone + offset logic for grid.
  [ ] Implement clone + rotate-around-center for circular.
  [ ] Add guard for max copy count (1000).
  [ ] Add ArrayPanel UI component (rows, columns, spacing inputs).
  [ ] Add unit tests for grid array.
  [ ] Add unit tests for circular array.
  [ ] Wire UI panel to commands via PropertiesPanel or dedicated dialog.

Done when:
  Grid array creates correct number of copies at correct positions.
  Circular array distributes copies evenly around center.
  Both commands are fully undoable.
  Unit tests pass for edge cases (1×1, single item, max count).
  UI allows user to configure and trigger both array types.
